  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sowing Opportunities for Youth Entrepreneurs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Young people from rural areas and smaller cities in Bolivia often wish to remain in their communities. However, the search for education and employment opportunities drives many to migrate to Bolivia&apos;s major cities or other countries. Local leaders are struggling to identify policies and fund programs to address this crisis. The IAF supports community-led solutions to expand economic opportunities for historically marginalized groups. IAF grantee Fundacin Trveris is a faith-based nonprofit working with a youth network and civil society, private, and public sector organizations dedicated to reducing poverty in rural Bolivia, especially for youth, women, and people with disabilities. Fundacin Trveris will build young people&apos;s skills in in-demand trades and entrepreneurial skills, develop new and strengthen existing partnerships that promote youth-focused public policies and programs, and provide training and technical assistance to strengthen youth-led enterprises.</narrative>
  </description>
